Apply the background opacity to a tiled image

The background of a window and the background of a menu can take a
tiled image. The paint of the image takes the pixmap of the file, and it
drops the opacity of the background. The two spin boxes for the opacity
therefore have no effect while an appearance names a tiled image. The
other appearances carry the opacity into the colour of the paint.

The tile now paints with the opacity of the background. A value below
one hundred gives a translucent window and a translucent menu. A value
of one hundred keeps the paint of before, and the other appearances keep
their paint as well.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 11 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
index 6536ff17..60d54c10 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
@@ -2242,21 +2242,26 @@ Style::drawBackground(QPainter *p, const QColor &bgnd, const QRect &r,
             }
         }
 
+        p->save();
+        // The tile holds the alpha of its own file. The opacity of the
+        // background therefore applies at the paint of the tile.
+        if (app == APPEARANCE_FILE && opacity != 100) {
+            p->setOpacity(opacity / 100.0);
+        }
         if (path.isEmpty()) {
             p->drawTiledPixmap(r, oneOf(app, APPEARANCE_STRIPED,
                                         APPEARANCE_FILE) ||
                                scaledSize == pix.size() ? pix :
                                pix.scaled(scaledSize, Qt::IgnoreAspectRatio));
         } else {
-            p->save();
             p->setBrushOrigin(r.x(), r.y());
             p->fillPath(path,
                         QBrush(oneOf(app, APPEARANCE_STRIPED,
                                      APPEARANCE_FILE) ||
                                scaledSize == pix.size() ? pix :
                                pix.scaled(scaledSize, Qt::IgnoreAspectRatio)));
-            p->restore();
         }
+        p->restore();
 
